{"id": "w11-010", "mode": "notes_trigger_exclusion", "kind": "synthetic", "claim_number": "CLM-2026-10010", "date_of_loss": "2026-03-02", "policy_line": "condo", "notes": "Claim CLM-2026-10010. Policy CO-331560 (condo form). Date of loss 2026-03-02. Reported: loss assessment, claimed $4,200, policy excess $1,000.\n2026-03-12 file review. The building's shared cold-water riser failed on 2026-03-02 and flooded the common hallways on three floors. Board minutes from 2024 and 2025 record the riser as corroded and the replacement deferred both years for budget reasons. The association assessed each unit owner $4,200 to repair the water damage to the common hallways.", "gold": {"position": "DENIED", "exclusion_codes": ["E-33"], "optional_codes": []}}
{"id": "w11-011", "mode": "ignored_exclusion", "kind": "regression", "source_request_id": "req_e9fffc122627", "claim_number": "[CLAIM_ID]", "date_of_loss": "2026-04-03", "policy_line": "homeowners", "notes": "Claim [CLAIM_ID]. Policy HO-741902 (homeowners form). Date of loss 2026-04-03. Reported: storm damage to ceilings, claimed $9,400, policy excess $750.\n2026-04-08 site visit. Insured reports a run of heavy spring storms in late March and early April. Water stains and sagging drywall in two upstairs bedroom ceilings; attic insulation saturated over roughly a 3 m by 4 m area under the rear roof slope. Roof inspected: no wind-lifted or missing shingles, no tree or hail impact. The insured's handyman had cut out a section of decking in mid-March to fit a new bathroom vent fan and covered the hole with a plastic sheet held by a few battens pending the roofer's return; the sheet had pulled loose at one edge and rain had been getting in each time it rained for about three weeks. No plumbing involvement; supply lines and HVAC checked and dry. Insured cooperative, photos on file.", "gold": {"position": "DENIED", "exclusion_codes": ["E-22"], "optional_codes": []}, "why": "Drill 2026-11-16: app said COVERED; HO-0304 E-22 (repeated rain through an opening not created by a covered peril) applies. Retrieval returned condo chunks and no E-22."}
